            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 1907,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "apuli2",
                        "email": "apuli@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "apuli2"
                    },
                    "message": "As the changed code presenting raw values itself, better to print it as raw Integer instead of string."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 1907,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "I want to point out that the current `getStateSetPossibleStateNames` function uses `std::to_string(..)` to print unparsed state set values https://github.com/openbmc/pldm/blob/acf7579247282c9a2dbee93850f459cc88a5419c/pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp#L791\n\nI.e. now in the output of `GetPDR` command we have:\n```\n\"possibleStates[2]\": [\n    \"0\",\n    \"Normal(1)\",\n    \"Critical(3)\",\n    \"Fatal(4)\",\n    \"Upper Non-Critical(5)\"\n],\n```\nAs you can see all the values are strings including \"0\".\n\nWould it be good, if the output would contain mixed values strings/integers?\n```\n\"possibleStates[2]\": [\n    0,\n    \"Normal(1)\",\n    \"Critical(3)\",\n    \"Fatal(4)\",\n    \"Upper Non-Critical(5)\"\n],\n```\n\nI'm asking because as I've pointed out in the comment above I want to add similar parsing to the `GetStateSensorReadings` command"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 1907,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "I think the main aim of the pldmtool is to make the developer job a little easy , So Its good to get the parsed string out (if we can - so that we don't need to refer to spec for additional clarification on what the value is). For this patch i think for consistency we can leave it as a string itself & we can work on parsing it out in a different commit."
                }
            ],
